Hi Kerubo 

I understand this has been listed as critical urgency. {color:#0747a6}Please confirm that you are comfortable with my approach.{color}

As it is for the supply of WiFi services (not a high risk negotiation) and the provider has its standard terms of service, my feeling is that there is little reason to insist on many amendments or that the service provider would be willing to change its standard terms for a 15k a year deal. I would point this out to customer. 

I have put it in ChatGPT against the playbook and it did identify some risk areas:
Warranties - does contain general warranties but not as comprehensive as Bolt;
Limitation of Liability - realistically seems unlikely a WiFi service provider would be willing to take on increased liability;
Indemnity - mutual indemnity is present but lacks specificity.

In the circumstances, I would just request that the 50% minimum term requirement and termination charges +(clause 7.2.ii)+ are removed from the termination clause, and if not accepted to get clarity from the provider whether the 90 days notice can only be given following the Minimum Service Term or falls within the Minimum Service Term.

Número de referência atribuído: *AMT-Q-1750286632*

