Dear [~accountid:618d20acfba4d0006ae30dd3] 

Please find the updated responses below:

+*Q.:*+ Regarding the data controller status — you mentioned that you are the data controller. Please justify this by specifying the legal basis under which you assume this role (e.g., legal obligation). Is there a legal act or an explanation from the State Data Protection Inspectorate on this matter? According to the provisions of the General Data Protection Regulation (GDPR) 2016/679, EDPS guidelines, and considering the purpose — that you are acting in our interests and on our behalf as the data controller — we believe your status, in the context of our agreement, should be that of a data processor.

{color:#bf2600}+*A.:*+{color}{color:#bf2600} Bolt acts as an independent data controller when providing services to business customers. This role is clearly defined in Section 4 of the Bolt Business General Terms and Conditions, which states that Bolt and the business customer are separate and independent controllers with respect to their respective processing of personal data.{color}

{color:#bf2600}Bolt determines the purposes and means of processing personal data needed to operate its platform. In this role, Bolt assumes full responsibility for its processing activities and ensures compliance with applicable data protection laws, including the GDPR.{color}

{color:#bf2600}The controller status is further supported by the {color}[{color:#bf2600}*EDPB Guidelines 07/2020*{color}|https://www.edpb.europa.eu/our-work-tools/our-documents/guidelines/guidelines-072020-concepts-controller-and-processor-gdpr_en]{color:#bf2600} on the concepts of controller and processor in the GDPR. In particular, p. 27, para. 82 illustrates the principle using a “Taxi service” example. While Bolt operates as an online platform rather than providing taxi services directly, the example still effectively clarifies the logic underpinning the controller relationship.{color}

{color:#bf2600}Additionally, Bolt is ISO/IEC 27001 certified, confirming that it meets international standards for information security management, and applies robust technical and organisational measures in line with Articles 24 and 32 GDPR.{color}

{color:#bf2600}In summary, both contractual terms and the factual circumstances of processing support Bolt’s position as an independent data controller. Each party — Bolt and the business customer — remains individually responsible for GDPR compliance, including providing privacy notices, establishing legal bases, and facilitating data subject rights.{color}

+*Q.:*+ What personal data of our employees will be used on the platform (name, surname, phone number, travel location, etc.)?

{color:#bf2600}+*A.:*+{color}{color:#bf2600} _In the Bolt Business platform, the business customer is required to provide the phone number and name of the users of Bolt Business services to register them. Optionally, Bolt User ID and email can be added._{color}

{color:#bf2600}_Bolt will also store and make available to the business customer the information on trip details, such as pick up and drop off location._ {color}

+*Q.:*+ Will video surveillance or audio recording be carried out inside the vehicle?

{color:#bf2600}+*A.:*+{color}{color:#bf2600} {color}{color:#bf2600}Bolt does not record video or audio inside vehicles by default. The only exception is the {color}[{color:#bf2600}*audio trip recording*{color}|https://bolt.eu/en/blog/audio-trip-recording-feature/]{color:#bf2600} feature available in the Bolt app as part of our safety toolkit. This feature may be activated by the rider or driver during a trip if they feel unsafe. Bolt only accesses such recordings if shared with Customer Support as part of an incident report.{color}

{color:#bf2600}Drivers may independently use video or audio recording devices, including where required by local law. In such cases, drivers act independently of Bolt and are solely responsible for compliance with data protection and transparency obligations.{color}

+*Q.:*+ Will the data mentioned in question 2 be shared with your appointed processors, sub-processors, or third parties?

{color:#bf2600}+*A.:*+{color}{color:#bf2600} {color}{color:#bf2600}_Personal data may be transferred to, stored and/or processed by Bolt Group Companies, subcontractors and partners when performing contractual obligations outside the country where you, as a client, are located. Please see here Bolt Group Companies table for details of third parties and countries where personal data may be transferred to:_ {color}[https://bolt.eu/en/privacy/privacy-controller-list/?category=rides|https://bolt.eu/en/privacy/privacy-controller-list/?category=rides|smart-link] {color:#bf2600}.{color}

+*Q.:*+ Will the data be transferred outside the EU?

