Hi [~accountid:62a7061fbf7afc006f3a8000] [~accountid:712020:02e8ad5d-a35d-44b9-b445-6111cdb230dc] jumping in to support from a privacy POV while [~accountid:712020:910c9a84-3532-4a39-97d2-4aee154ce8df] is OOO.

{panel:bgColor=#deebff}
*General overview/points to consider*
{panel}

* About filming the passengers: I think the approach to still record non-consenting riders and delete the recording after is not privacy-friendly. With this approach, we’re risking to get complaints, and as we’re facilitating such a category, it will be hard to limit our liability unless that’s explicitly covered by our agreement (CC [~accountid:712020:02e8ad5d-a35d-44b9-b445-6111cdb230dc] )
* Regarding children - Aivis must be extremely careful and record only when they have a written approval from a parent/guardian. Suggest not filing rides with children by default.

{panel:bgColor=#deebff}
*Agreement* 
{panel}

[~accountid:712020:02e8ad5d-a35d-44b9-b445-6111cdb230dc] I understand you’re drafting the partnership agreement - can you please share it in a Google Docs format once it’s drafted? I will then add the necessary privacy wording that I already have available. Since no heavy personal data sharing is happening, I’ll add some light-touch clauses.

{panel:bgColor=#deebff}
*Suggested wording for disclaimer*
{panel}

I have prepared a couple of versions for the disclaimer to be shown to passengers -  a shorter version, and a longer one. Can we ensure that the disclaimer is displayed before the ride is booked by the rider?

In addition to that, I suggest adding an email address/contact persons details for cases when the riders want to escalate issues/raise concerns/revoke their consent or object to the recordings being published.

{quote}*Celebrity Taxi rides are filmed for entertainment purposes.*
